__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
node_modules
.DS_Store

# Vite build output for the dashboard SPA.
#
# Ignored the way the CRM and Helpdesk apps ignore theirs. What makes that safe
# is the `package.json` at the app root: `bench get-app` runs
# `yarn install --check-files` there, `postinstall` builds both, and the route
# then has a template to render. Without that root package.json a fresh clone
# has the route rule and no page to render, which is a 404 on the dashboard.
# `tests/test_installable.py` holds the manifest so the two cannot come apart.
tally_connector/public/frontend/
tally_connector/www/tally_connector.html
frontend/auto-imports.d.ts

# The root package.json declares no dependencies of its own - it exists so that
# `bench get-app` has a postinstall hook to run - so its lockfile carries no
# information and only ever shows up as noise in a diff.
/yarn.lock

# Throwaway diagnostics.
#
# A one-off script that reproduces a defect has to live inside the app to be
# importable by `bench execute`, which puts it right where `git add -A` will
# sweep it up. That has now happened four times, and each was caught by the
# pre-push scan rather than by remembering - twice after the push had already
# gone. Remembering is not the fix; the pattern is.
#
# Anything worth keeping becomes a test, which is where it can fail on its own.
tally_connector/_*.py
